Grok 1.0.62 live composer evidence for PR kunchenguid/firstmate#6132
Captured 2026-10-20 on zeppola, tmux 3.6a, against the real grok CLI.

Provenance:
- grok 1.0.62 (1474f9cbdd91) [stable], the machine's existing login. No credential was copied,
  requested, or synthesized; no sign-in, sign-out, or credential-store edit was performed.
- Launch: grok --always-approve --reasoning-effort high, as the session command on the private
  fm-lab tmux socket inside a marked disposable lab home (bin/fm-lab-home.sh), from the PR
  worktree, at 120x40. No model prompt was ever submitted, so no model tokens were spent.
- Every verdict below comes from the REAL Firstmate terminal interface (bin/fm-tmux-lib.sh:
  fm_tmux_composer_state, fm_pane_input_pending) and the REAL dispatcher
  (bin/fm-backend.sh: fm_backend_composer_state tmux) reading a real captured tmux pane.
- The "cursorless" rows re-read the very same captured pane through the herdr (styled=1) and
  cmux/orca (styled=0) capability profiles, which is how every non-tmux backend reads it.
  Those are capability-profile re-reads of a real capture, not launches of Herdr/cmux/orca.
- The controlled-terminal-input rows at the end are real tmux panes rendering a written fixture.
  They exercise the runtime input path, not a Grok release's own rendering, and are labelled as
  controlled inputs.

